// timing + entropy both come from the L2 clock — no L1 wait, no state-override probe.`}),e.jsx(h,{variant:"amber",title:"Investor disclosure",children:"Users and liquidity providers should understand that every game carries this sequencer trust assumption. It is a deliberate, disclosed trade-off of building on a fast L2 — not a hidden one — and it is bounded by the same hard payout caps that protect every pool."})]}),e.jsxs(n,{id:"security",title:"9 · Security Model",eyebrow:"Defence in depth",children:[e.jsx(s,{children:"The protocol is built on defence-in-depth: independent safety layers so that no single failure is catastrophic. Every state-changing external function is protected by a reentrancy guard, every token movement uses OpenZeppelin SafeERC20, and Solidity 0.8's checked arithmetic removes overflow and underflow classes entirely."}),e.jsx(x,{head:["Attack vector","Mitigation"],rows:[["Double-reveal / replay","A settled flag makes any bet settle exactly once; duplicate reveals revert."],["Cross-player / cross-block mixing","Multi-reveal requires all bets share one player and one commit block."],["Reveal front-running","Anyone may reveal, but payout is hard-bound to the original bettor; a front-runner only pays gas."],["Stale-bet manipulation","Past the reveal window a bet can only expire (forced loss, closed automatically); waiting is never profitable."],["Pool drain","Worst-case payout, bet caps, win caps and a live solvency check are enforced before locking a bet."]]}),e.jsx(y,{children:"Owner trust model"}),e.jsx(s,{children:"Each game has an owner (its creator) who can tune configuration within hard bounds (staker fee ≤ 10%, RTP up to the game's on-chain ceiling — 98% for fair games, higher where the raw game edge is larger), pause new bets, and withdraw only their own stake. A change never affects a bet already placed. Owners cannot alter outcomes, cannot touch other stakers' funds, and cannot trap pending bets — reveal, unstake and expiry remain callable even while paused. Players and LPs choose which games to join knowing the owner address."}),e.jsx(h,{variant:"blue",title:"Standards coverage",children:"The contracts are checked against the OWASP Smart Contract Top 10 — reentrancy (guarded), arithmetic (0.8 checked), unchecked returns (SafeERC20), access control (owner-bounded), front-running (commit-reveal), denial-of-service (bounded loops and pagination), randomness (commit-reveal + SHA-256), flash loans (cross-block commit-reveal), and tx.origin (never used). An internal security review accompanies this paper; the architecture is prepared for formal third-party audit — minimal trust surface, no upgradeable proxies in the game path, and full event coverage for every state change."})]}),e.jsxs(n,{id:"economics",title:`10 · Protocol Economics — $${l}`,eyebrow:"The flywheel",children:[e.jsx(s,{children:"Value in the protocol flows along three rails. Every bet pays a 1% platform fee (adjustable, never above 2%) to the protocol treasury; 1% goes to the creator who launched the game; and the game's own staker fee stays in its pool, compounding into the stakers' share value. Opening a game is free. All splits are enforced on-chain and visible in events."}),e.jsxs(s,{children:[e.jsxs("b",{className:"text-bone-100",children:["$",l]})," is a flat, fixed-supply platform token — no rebase, no decay. Platform fees land in the ",e.jsx("b",{className:"text-bone-100",children:"ElcasTreasury"})," contract, which can only",e.jsxs("b",{className:"text-bone-100",children:[" buy $",l," and burn it"]})," — it has no withdraw function, swaps only through a fixed ETH/$",l," pool (other fee tokens need a route that waits two days before it can be used), and pays its keeper nothing beyond measured gas. Burned $",l," is permanently removed from circulation. This is the flywheel: casino activity generates fees, fees buy back $",l,", and the buyback is burned — aligning long-term holders with total protocol activity. Because every fee, split and payout emits an indexed event, the entire economy is measurable from chain data alone."]}),e.jsx(A,{caption:"The ELCAS flywheel — casino fees buy back and burn the token",children:e.jsxs("svg",{viewBox:"0 0 640 120",className:"w-full h-auto",fill:"none",children:[[{x:20,c:"#34d399",t:"casino fees ($)"},{x:190,c:"#fbbf24",t:`buy back $${l}`},{x:360,c:"#cd202a",t:`burn $${l}`},{x:520,c:"#b4ff2e",t:"supply ↓ · value ↑"}].map((a,o)=>e.jsxs("g",{children:[e.jsx("rect",{x:a.x,y:"40",width:"120",height:"44",rx:"10",fill:"#12161d",stroke:a.c,strokeWidth:"1.4"}),e.jsx("text",{x:a.x+60,y:"66",textAnchor:"middle",fill:a.c,fontSize:"11",fontWeight:"700",fontFamily:"monospace",children:a.t}),o<3&&e.jsx("path",{d:`M${a.x+120} 62 L${a.x+170} 62`,stroke:"#6b7f96",strokeWidth:"1.5",markerEnd:"url(#wpf)"})]},o)),e.jsx("defs",{children:e.jsx("marker",{id:"wpf",markerWidth:"9",markerHeight:"9",refX:"6",refY:"3",orient:"auto",children:e.jsx("path",{d:"M0 0 L6 3 L0 6 z",fill:"#6b7f96"})})})]})}),e.jsx(D,{items:["Fixed supply","Buyback & burn","No decay","On-chain fee rails","Live flywheel analytics"]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{id:"data",title:"11 · Traction & Verifiable Data",eyebrow:"Don't trust — verify",children:[e.jsxs(s,{children:["The protocol is measured, not marketed. Every bet, fee split, stake, launch and burn emits an indexed on-chain event, so the entire economy can be reconstructed by anyone from public chain data — no privileged dashboard and no self-reported figure. The core contracts below are the anchor for any due-diligence; all are verifiable on the ",c.name," explorer."]}),e.jsx("div",{className:"my-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-ink-700/70 scrollbar-hide",children:e.jsxs("table",{className:"w-full min-w-[420px] border-collapse text-[13px]",children:[e.jsx("thead",{children:e.jsxs("tr",{className:"bg-ink-850/70",children:[e.jsx("th",{className:"border-b border-ink-700 px-3.5 py-2.5 text-left text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-bone-400",child